$$
49a + 7b + c = 49a + 7b - a - b = 48a + 6b \tag{4}
$$

So:
$$
50 < 48a + 6b < 60 \tag{5}
$$

#### Substitute into $ 64a + 8b + c = f(8) $:

$$
64a + 8b + c = 64a + 8b - a - b = 63a + 7b \tag{6}
$$

So:
$$
70 < 63a + 7b < 80 \tag{7}
$$

Now we have:

$$
50 < 48a + 6b < 60 \tag{5}
$$
$$
70 < 63a + 7b < 80 \tag{7}
$$

These two inequalities will help us determine bounds for $ a $ and $ b $, and from there compute $ f(100) $.

---

### **Step 4: Simplify and analyze the inequalities**

